  "_comment": [
    "CANONICAL catalog parser rules — the single source of truth.",
    "app/assets/catalog/parsers.json is GENERATED from this file by",
    "tools/gen_catalog_assets.py; tools/ci_gates.sh fails CI when they diverge.",
    "Edit here, regenerate, never hand-edit the asset.",
    "Amount scale is {1,3} per migration 0091 (2- and 3-decimal currencies).",
    "",
    "SNB (...101): the currency token is REQUIRED immediately before the amount.",
    "With it optional the masked card number was captured as the transaction",
    "amount — reproduced against the anonymized fixture",
    "known_bank_known_merchant_auto_confirm (4521 instead of 45.00) and confirmed",
    "on research/sms_model_lab real-holdout records.",
    "KNOWN LIMITATION, found in review: this verifies only the ARABIC layout",
    "('مبلغ:SAR 45.00', currency before amount). The real ENGLISH layout is",
    "'Amount 8 SAR' — currency AFTER the amount — which this pattern no longer",
    "matches at all. That is fail-closed (no match, heuristics take over) rather",
    "than wrong money, and nothing is live because no parser is servable and the",
    "bundle now seeds inactive. A pattern accepting currency on EITHER side is",
    "required before ...101 could be promoted.",
    "",
    "Riyad (...103): UNCHANGED. The same pattern shape, but the defect could not",
    "be reproduced and the real Riyad layout is 'مبلغ:700.00 SAR' — currency",
    "AFTER the amount — so the SNB fix would have made the rule never match.",
    "A money rule is not changed on resemblance. Tracked as an open risk: the",
    "card line precedes the amount line, so the first Riyad message carrying a",
    "لدى/At anchor would capture the card suffix."
